{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784306813,"nonce":"EMw+14aT/1E7vr+pzIqcWYarekg=","title":"[dogfood] clone token over-asks contents:write -\u003e 422, silently falls back to anonymous","message":"mint_checkout_credential (scarab-forge-github/src/lib.rs ~731) requests an installation token with permissions {contents: write} for non-fork runs (read only for fork PRs). When the App grants only contents:read, GitHub returns:\n\n  422 'The level of access for permissions requested are not granted to this installation.'\n\nscarab logs a WARN and falls back to an ANONYMOUS clone. That only works because thulasi-ram/scarab-ci is public — on a PRIVATE repo the checkout would fail. So the 'private-repo clone with a minted installation token' path (a HUMAN VERIFY item) is NOT actually exercised here; every dogfood clone has been anonymous.\n\nA checkout only READS the tree — it should request {contents: read} regardless of fork status. Requesting write forces every install to grant contents:write to the CI App (broad) just to clone. Fix: request contents:read for the clone credential; reserve write for steps that actually push. Reproduced on the in-cluster Helm dogfood (App had contents:read); host-binary run likely also fell back to anonymous (public repo masked it).","files":null}]}